Step 2: Send a Secret Message Between Screens

We are going to use the first window to beam a message directly into the second window.
In your first terminal, type the following command (make sure to replace /dev/pts/1 with whatever number your second window actually showed):
bash
echo "Hello from the other screen!" > /dev/pts/1
Use code with caution.
Press Enter, and look at your second window—the text will instantly pop up there as if by magic!

